<div class="pagehead">
<p class="eyebrow">Speaking</p>
<h1>A human on the podium.</h1>
<p class="dek">Russ Michaels speaks on AI, authorship, and self-government &mdash; which decisions belong in human hands, and why.</p>
</div>

<hr class="rule" />

<section class="speaking">
<h2 class="sec">The keynote</h2>
<p class="talk-meta">SXSW 2027 PanelPicker proposal &middot; community voting closed Aug 23 &middot; Austin &middot; Tech &amp; AI</p>
<p class="talk-title">Who Sings the &ldquo;We&rdquo;? Optimized Out of Your Own World</p>
<div class="prose"><p>Quincy Jones hung a sign over the biggest voices in the world &mdash; <em>check your ego at the door</em> &mdash; and they made a song no perfect singer could. Put today&rsquo;s AI in that studio and every note is flawless. So is the danger: a partner so good you hand over your part, one choice at a time, until the decision quietly stops being yours &mdash; and you never feel it leave. The law&rsquo;s name for a choice that&rsquo;s yours in name only is undue influence. Which decisions do you keep? Check your ego. Keep your voice.</p></div>
<ul class="steps" style="margin-top:8px">
<li>The undue-influence test &mdash; run live on your own AI-assisted decisions.</li>
<li>Silent Deferral &mdash; how authorship transfers with no alarm, no villain, no bad result.</li>
<li>Autotune for your judgment &mdash; perfect pitch, no range, and why range is the point.</li>
<li>Self-government &mdash; what to hand off, and what stays in human hands.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<h2 class="sec">Formats</h2>
<section class="cols">
<div><h3>Keynote</h3><p>A 20&ndash;45 minute keynote for technology, ideas, and leadership stages.</p></div>
<div><h3>Panels &amp; fireside</h3><p>AI and human agency, the future of professional judgment, law &amp; technology.</p></div>
<div><h3>Private rooms</h3><p>Boards, partnerships, and teams working out what to hand to the machine &mdash; and what to keep.</p></div>
</section>

